    "turn_text": "Fellows, we are incredibly excited to welcome Congressman Robert C. Bobby Scott to Ed's Not Dead. Congressman Scott is represented Virginia's third congressional district in the U.S. House of Representatives since 1993. Prior to his service in Congress, he served 15 years in the Virginia General Assembly. Congressman Scott currently serves as a chairman of the Committee on Education and Labor. In this position, he's advancing an agenda that improves equity in education, free students from the burdens of crippling debt, protects and expands access to affordable healthcare, ensures workers have a safe workplace, where they can earn a living wage, free from discrimination, and guarantees seniors have a secure and dignified retirement. Welcome to Ed's Not Dead Chairman Scott. We are indeed excited and honored to have you on the show. So let's jump right into our interview. I know that you've had a lot going on in the last 24 hours and we're going to get to talk about that. But where are we as a public education system today nationally amidst the current public health emergency or crisis that we're in?",
