    "turn_text": "The problem we have now is that we've heard a lot about how the pandemic has exacerbated preexisting health conditions. Those with the preexisting health conditions have been more adversely affected by the pandemic than others. We're also finding out that those who have been at the bottom of the achievement gap have been more adversely affected than others. with distance learning. If you're at the bottom of the achievement gap, you're probably less likely to even have a computer, less likely to have connectivity or have poor connectivity at home. So all of the problems in education have been exacerbated by the pandemic and just made matters worse. And so we have a lot of catching up to do. This group would be familiar with the summer slide where low-income students leave in June, come back two months worse. By September, they're two months worse off than they left. Well, we've been sliding for about eight to 10 months. And so we have a lot of catching up to do. And so the pandemic has just made those matters worse. The other students, some students have done okay with distance learning. They've been able to keep up And those at the bottom of the achievement gap have just been horrible. And special education students, it's been a disaster. We have a lot of catching up to do there.",
