    "turn_text": "Well, it's substantial portion of that would be K through 12, about $58 billion. And it's distributed to a large extent based on the Title I formula, so land where it's actually needed. A relatively significant portion will go to private schools and not to public schools where it's most needed. But if you want the bill passed, sometimes you just have to put up with. But it's there and the school systems will use the money. to make up for the deficits. There's a lot of catching up that needs to be done. I'd like for additional funding to take place to make sure that school systems can cancel summer vacation. We can't afford to take two more months off, inflict another summer slide where the students start regressing all over again. We need to use that time to catch up. You can't cancel a summer vacation for free. That's going to cost money. And I'd like to see the federal government step up and make sure that that's happening. There's a lot of catching up to do for those at the bottom of achievement gaps and for special education students. So there's a lot of work that's to be done. And that's not free. The federal government has to step up because the state and local governments across the country are very much stressed already.",
